{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2159-01-21 04:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, I'm Dr. Lee, one of your hospital doctors. You were brought in with chest pain. Can you tell me what happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2159-01-21 04:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I had a tight, heavy feeling in my chest—right in the middle. It scared me. I also felt nauseous and threw up a little."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2159-01-21 04:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Your ECG showed some changes, and your potassium was high—6.6. That can cause chest discomfort and even heart rhythm issues. We gave you treatment to bring it down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2159-01-21 04:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. Is my heart okay? I’ve had heart surgery before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2159-01-21 04:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your heart is stable. Your recent cath showed your grafts are open. The chest pain is likely from fluid buildup because your dialysis hasn’t been fully clearing everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2159-01-21 04:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. My left arm fistula hasn’t been working well lately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2159-01-21 04:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’re going to evaluate your fistula with a special test called a fistulogram. It checks blood flow and looks for blockages."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2159-01-21 04:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that fix it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2159-01-21 04:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It helps us decide what to do next. If there’s a narrowing, we might open it up during the same procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2159-01-21 04:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I trust you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2159-01-21 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs are improving. Potassium is down to 5.9, and your chest pain is gone. We’ll hold off on dialysis until tomorrow morning unless things change."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2159-01-21 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. But my INR is high—6.8? I take warfarin for my mechanical valve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2159-01-21 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s concerning. But cardiology says we can hold warfarin for now and restart it when it’s safer. You’re not at high risk for clots during this short break."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2159-01-21 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t been taking it regularly. I ran out for a few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2159-01-21 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That likely explains the high INR. We’ll adjust your dose when we restart it. For now, we’re focused on stabilizing your potassium and fluid levels."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2159-01-22 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You had dialysis yesterday, and your symptoms are better. We’re planning the fistulogram tomorrow to check your access."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2159-01-22 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it safe? I’ve had issues with my fistula before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2159-01-22 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s generally safe. But because of your history, there’s a small risk of bleeding or damage. We’ll monitor closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2159-01-26 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We just finished the fistulogram. There was a significant narrowing in your jump graft. We tried to open it with a balloon, but it caused a rupture and bleeding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2159-01-26 09:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh no! Is that serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2159-01-26 09:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It is, but we acted quickly. Surgery was called, and they evacuated the hematoma. Your arm is stable now, but the fistula can’t be used anymore."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2159-01-26 09:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So how will I get dialysis?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2159-01-26 09:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We placed a temporary line in your right subclavian vein. It’s working well. Soon, we’ll switch it to a tunneled line for longer-term use."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2159-01-26 09:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need a new fistula?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2159-01-26 09:43:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. You’ll follow up with transplant surgery to create a new one on your right arm. That side must be protected—no blood draws or IVs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2159-01-26 09:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. No poking on the right arm."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2159-01-26 17:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The radiology team just placed a tunneled dialysis line in your right internal jugular vein. It’s more secure and meant for longer use."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2159-01-26 17:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it safe there? I have a mechanical valve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2159-01-26 17:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s a common site. We avoided the left side since we may need that for future access. The line is in good position."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2159-01-27 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs are improving. Potassium is 5.0, creatinine down to 6.1. Your chest pain hasn’t returned, and your heart rhythm is stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2159-01-27 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. What about my warfarin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2159-01-27 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re restarting it at a lower dose—5 mg instead of 6 mg. Your INR is now in a safer range. We’ll monitor it closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2159-01-27 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I take it at the same time every day?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2159-01-27 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, ideally in the evening. And take your other meds as prescribed—especially the blood pressure and cholesterol pills."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2159-01-27 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My arm feels better. No swelling or pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2159-01-27 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. The surgical site is healing well. No signs of infection. Your hand is warm, pulses are strong."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2159-01-27 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2159-01-27 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, likely tomorrow. We’ll do one more procedure to secure your dialysis line fully."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2159-01-28 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What’s happening this morning?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2159-01-28 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re converting your temporary line to a permanent tunneled catheter. It’s a quick procedure, done under imaging guidance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2159-01-28 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Same spot?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2159-01-28 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Same vein, but it’s tunneled under the skin, which reduces infection risk and makes it more stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2159-01-28 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The procedure went smoothly. Your new tunneled line is in place and ready for dialysis. You’re doing really well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2159-01-28 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2159-01-28 12:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep the dressing clean and dry. Watch for redness, swelling, or drainage. Weigh yourself daily—call us if you gain more than 3 pounds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2159-01-28 12:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2159-01-28 12:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue all your usual medications. Warfarin 5 mg daily, aspirin, blood pressure meds, and the ones for your bones and stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2159-01-28 12:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I have pain in my arm from the surgery. Can I take something?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2159-01-28 12:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re prescribing hydrocodone for breakthrough pain. Take it only as needed, not more than every 6 hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2159-01-28 12:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2159-01-28 12:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll see transplant surgery next week to plan your new fistula. Also, nephrology and cardiology for ongoing management."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2159-01-28 12:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No blood draws on my right arm, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2159-01-28 12:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. That arm is reserved for your future fistula. Use the left side for any blood work or IVs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2159-01-28 12:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my INR? When should I check it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2159-01-28 12:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Get it checked in 3 days, then weekly until it’s stable. Goal is between 2.5 and 3.5."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2159-01-28 12:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make sure to do that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2159-01-28 12:43:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great. We’ll have your discharge papers ready soon. You can go home today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2159-01-28 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel much better. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2159-01-28 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Remember: watch your weight, protect your right arm, take your meds, and keep your follow-up appointments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2159-01-28 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’m ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2159-01-28 13:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The nurse will go over your instructions one more time, and then you’re all set."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2159-01-28 13:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, sounds good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2159-01-28 13:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, and call us if anything changes—especially chest pain, shortness of breath, or issues with your dialysis line."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2159-01-28 13:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2159-01-28 13:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Stay consistent with your care, and you’ll stay stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2159-01-28 13:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do my best."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2159-01-28 13:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s all we ask. The nurse will be in shortly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2159-01-28 13:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright, I’m ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2159-01-28 13:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Have a safe trip home. We’ll see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2159-01-28 13:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2159-01-28 13:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You're welcome. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2159-01-28 13:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2159-01-28 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The discharge nurse will be in soon to review everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2159-01-28 13:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2159-01-28 13:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve made great progress. Keep up the good work."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2159-01-28 13:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2159-01-28 13:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You're very welcome. Stay healthy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2159-01-28 13:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2159-01-28 13:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll be in touch with your outpatient team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2159-01-28 13:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good to know."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2159-01-28 13:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take it easy at home. Rest and recover."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2159-01-28 13:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I plan to."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2159-01-28 13:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll see you soon in clinic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2159-01-28 13:52:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Looking forward to it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2159-01-28 13:54:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Have a safe journey home."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2159-01-21 04:19:00",
    "admission_end": "2159-01-28 15:20:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with end-stage renal disease on hemodialysis was admitted with chest pain and hyperkalemia. Initial evaluation revealed fluid overload and elevated potassium, managed with medical therapy and dialysis. Her left arm arteriovenous fistula, previously complicated by steal syndrome, was evaluated with a fistulogram, which revealed stenosis. During attempted angioplasty, the fistula ruptured, causing a hematoma that required surgical evacuation. The fistula was rendered nonfunctional, and a temporary right subclavian dialysis line was placed, later converted to a tunneled catheter. Her chest pain resolved, potassium normalized, and INR stabilized after warfarin adjustment. She was discharged home with instructions to protect her right arm for future fistula creation, continue medications, monitor weight, and follow up with transplant surgery and nephrology.",
    "problems": [
      "Hyperpotassemia",
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Complications of transplanted kidney",
      "Hypertensive chronic kidney disease, unspecified, with chronic kidney disease stage V or end stage renal disease",
      "Chronic diastolic heart failure",
      "Congestive heart failure, unspecified",
      "Other complications due to renal dialysis device, implant, and graft",
      "Hematoma complicating a procedure",
      "Other chest pain",
      "Kidney dialysis as the cause of abnormal reaction of patient, or of later complication, without mention of misadventure at time of procedure",
      "Abnormal coagulation profile",
      "Disorders of phosphorus metabolism",
      "Coronary atherosclerosis of unspecified type of vessel, native or graft",
      "Aortocoronary bypass status",
      "Percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty status",
      "Heart valve replaced by other means",
      "Personal history of transient ischemic attack (TIA), and cerebral infarction without residual deficits",
      "Peripheral vascular disease, unspecified",
      "Acquired absence of kidney",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Insomnia, unspecified",
      "Restless legs syndrome (RLS)",
      "Nontoxic multinodular goiter",
      "Personal history of tobacco use"
    ]
  }
}
